# Styled Dropdowns Required

- Never ship default browser dropdown styling in the web app.
- Every `<select>` must use the design system: explicit border, background, typography, spacing, focus style, and disabled style.
- Use `appearance-none` and provide a custom chevron indicator so Apple/native UI chrome does not appear.
- Dropdown containers should visually match adjacent controls (buttons/inputs) in shadow, border thickness, and color tokens.

## Example

```tsx
<div className="relative">
  <select className="appearance-none border-2 border-ink bg-paper px-3 py-2 pr-10 shadow-[4px_4px_0_0_#111111]">
    <option>Example</option>
  </select>
  <span className="pointer-events-none absolute right-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2">▾</span>
</div>
```

